WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
How to save an iPhone text conversation as a PDF with OpenExtract, free on Windows, Mac and Linux.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.938
OpenExtract's start screen lists the iPhone backups it finds on your computer. Click Open next to yours.

3
00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:16.452
If the backup is encrypted, type the password you set for it, and click Unlock. It stays on your computer.

4
00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:21.145
The backup's home page shows what's in it. Click Messages.

5
00:00:21.145 --> 00:00:33.463
Every conversation is listed, newest first. Click the one you want to save. It opens with its photos, dates and times.

6
00:00:33.463 --> 00:00:37.597
Click Save conversation, at the top right.

7
00:00:37.597 --> 00:00:42.701
Readable document, the PDF, is already chosen. Click Save.

8
00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:46.800
Pick a folder on your computer. The PDF is saved there, named after the conversation.

9
00:00:46.800 --> 00:01:00.300
The PDF has the whole conversation: every message with its date and time, who sent it, and the photos.

10
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.300
OpenExtract is free and open source, for Windows, Mac and Linux. Get it at openextract.app.
